FREEZE bug notice (render, not editing production): tegu_render_generic_spec_needs_sidecar currently forces a variant for compare/view-level/view-layer/view-format alias but NOT for b->flags (twin/shader-swizzle). If a plan has flags but no constants/view alias, selection falls back to default and the flags are silently lost before tegu_generic_v2_required sees the selected variant. Exact one-line fix for render_pipeline.inc (private patch; apply only if root wants before integration):
@@ const TeguAIRGraphicsSpecializationBinding *b=&spec->bindings[i];
+  if(b->flags)return 1;
   if(b->compare_enabled)return 1;
This makes selection build a variant; tegu_generic_v2_required then sees flags and forces v2, and tegu_generic_v2_build_job refuses flags explicitly (already implemented). No other change needed.
Also note: view_type/aspect are now in the synced header but render does not validate/consume them; nonzero view type/aspect remains an explicit gap. Current host tests do not exercise flags; all listed tests still PASS. No production write made after FREEZE.
